<title>UK: UK cattle slaughter to top one million - minister.</title>
<headline>UK cattle slaughter to top one million - minister.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain has now slaughtered almost one million cattle in its bid to take older animals out of the food chain and stamp out mad cow disease, Agriculture Minister Douglas Hogg said on Monday.</p>
<p>A 30-month cull was set up in May and Hogg told farming leaders that the current backlog should be cleared by Christmas.</p>
<p>&quot;More than 55,000 animals a week are now being slaughtered under the scheme,&quot; he told reporters. &quot;By the end of this week, more than a million cull cows, clean cattle and bulls, will have been slaughtered.&quot;</p>
<p>The European Union imposed a ban on British beef after scientists disclosed in March a probable link between mad cow disease, or Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy (BSE), and the fatal Creutzfeldt-Jakob Disease, which rots human brains.</p>
</text>
